 "short": "Hand slow work to a line of jobs that workers take in turn.",
 "what": "A message queue is a waiting line of small messages between two parts of a system. A producer adds a job and moves on; workers (consumers) take jobs one at a time and confirm each one when done. If traffic spikes, the line gets longer instead of servers falling over.",
 "analogy": "Order tickets in a restaurant kitchen. The waiter pins the order and goes back to the tables; cooks take the next ticket when their hands are free.",
